-- title:
--   Continuity of truncated cyclic outputs in the truncation endpoints
-- statement:
--   For functions $B,C$ on the plane and a kernel $K$, the cyclic kernel output is $\int_{\mathbb R}B(z_2,c)\,C(c,z_1)\,K(z_1+z_2+c)\,dc$, and the hard kernel is $H_{r,R}(t)=\mathbf 1_{r<|t|\le R}/t$. Let $z$ be a cubically slice-good point for $B,C$: the slices $c\mapsto B(z_2,c)$ and $c\mapsto C(c,z_1)$ are measurable with finite $L^3$ norms. Then for $0<r<R$ the truncated output
--   $$
--   (r',R')\longmapsto\int B(z_2,c)\,C(c,z_1)\,H_{r',R'}(z_1+z_2+c)\,dc
--   $$
--   is continuous at $(r,R)$.
--
--   This justifies restricting the supremum over truncations to rational endpoints.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/TriangularHilbert/EndpointContinuity.lean#L45-L87

